join "Ms Kim" left
set {kim.spoke} += 1.0
"Ms Kim": Oh, hello! Who might you be?
- A reporter.
- An old friend of Anthony's.
"Ms Kim": Well, that's nice, sweetheart.
"Ms Kim": I'm Ms. Kim. You can call me Ms. Kim.
- Alright, Ms. Kim.
"Ms Kim": Did you talk to Matilda?
if {matilda.spoke} > 0.0:
	- Yes, I did.
		if {matilda.reporter_reveal} == true:
			- She wasn't very nice.
				"Ms Kim": Ah, she can be prickly. Your best bet is to talk to Will and have him talk to her. She's stubborn, but she'd do anything for her husband.
				set {kim.will} = true
		else:
			- She's interesting.
				"Ms Kim": She's a character. She knows exactly what she wants and does her darndest to get it!
	"Ms Kim": Things have been hard for her. First Ant disappearing all those years ago, now Casper, too...
	"Ms Kim": The years haven't been easy on her.
	"Ms Kim": And, well... not to be a gossip...
	- Go on...
		"Ms Kim": Well, all I heard was that she's not in the will at all. After all those years with Ant, helping raise his son, and not to get a penny? It just seems a shame.
		"Ms Kim": Ah, but I've said too much! Don't let me keep you here! Plus, I need to get back to my book.
		- Wait! Before I go...
			- How do you know Anthony?
				"Ms Kim": He was my nephew. I lived in this house as a girl... I wanted to come back and see it again. Now, take care!
				[end_timeline]
			- Who else should I talk to?
				"Ms Kim": Gertrude has lived in this house with Casper since Anthony disappeared. She must know a lot about what goes on under its roof. Now, take care!
				set {kim.gertrude} = true
				[end_timeline]
else:
	- No, I haven't.
		"Ms Kim": Well, be careful. She's quick to put her hackles up. She doesn't like people prying into her life, especially after the news came poking around after Anthony's disappearence.
		- Good to know.
			"Ms Kim": And, well... Not to be a gossip, but...
			- Go on.
				"Ms Kim": Well, all I heard was that she's not in the will at all. After all those years with Ant, helping raise his son, and not to get a penny? It just seems a shame.
				"Ms Kim": Ah, but I've said too much! Don't let me keep you here! Plus, I need to get back to my book.
				- Wait! Before I go...
					- How do you know Anthony?
						"Ms Kim": He was my nephew. I lived in this house as a girl... I wanted to come back and see it again. Now, take care!
						[end_timeline]
					- Who else should I talk to?
						"Ms Kim": Gertrude has lived in this house with Casper since Anthony disappeared. She must know a lot about what goes on under its roof. Now, take care!
						[end_timeline]